{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456910-azaneal-reaching-demonhood","id":1456910,"title":"azaneal reaching demonhood","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-15T15:30:43-07:00","id":1456910,"title":"azaneal reaching demonhood","content":"Its mentioned in the wiki that he reached demonhood. Does anybody know how that happend?<br /> <br /> Also how powerful would he be once he became a demon? Are we talking ante level? Or possible even higher? Could he duke it out with Caine? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I never read up on demon lore so i am not sure how powerful demons are. I would presume as a newly made demon he wouldnt be high up the demon food chain. But still he transcended. That tells me his new form is far more powerful then he ever was as a vampire.<br /> <br /> There also seems to be a debate about his generation. Anything between second and fifth. Either way he was a powerful vampire. So is there any advantage if you reach demonhood, if you were a powerful vampire before? Would that put him higher in the new food chain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 08-15-2021, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T16:52:34-07:00","id":1456911,"title":"","content":"Sorry to be cliche, but the answer to all those questions is whatever the gm wants them to be. There isn't a cannon answer. He isn't a fallen however, that's for certain. <br /> I personally belive becoming a demon grants a &quot;hell&quot; of a lot of power, but also saddles the demon with far more restrictions on how it can use that power. Needing to be summoned, not having corporeal form, can't interact with mortals unless they give him permission or he was summoned. Etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T17:10:36-07:00","id":1456914,"title":"","content":"Azaneal and Mary the Black are both essentially &quot;here there be dragons&quot; characters, I think. Monsters like this are pretexts for never, ever commissioning writing on supplements that would take characters to certain locations until a novelist decides to send Beckett, Lucita, or Theo Bell there to save the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T21:34:36-07:00","id":1456927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456910-azaneal-reaching-demonhood?p=1456914#post1456914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Azaneal and Mary the Black are both essentially &quot;here there be dragons&quot; characters, I think. Monsters like this are pretexts for never, ever commissioning writing on supplements that would take characters to certain locations until a novelist decides to send Beckett, Lucita, or Theo Bell there to save the day.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Meh, somewhere between Michael from Constantinople by Night &amp; Huitzilopochtli from Chaos Factor, if someone wants to throw all the snowflakeness into the fan. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T06:47:45-07:00","id":1456962,"title":"","content":"I would imagine that he would remain within the confines of his Generation in terms of power. He likely punches above his weight, but he's no ante. I don't like the examples given for Diamonion 7+, but I really like 6, so I imagine 7+ as really a sort of demonization/apotheosis collection of powers. He can create contracts, collects faith. He can bestow investments. He has a bunch of investments ob himself, and perhaps he can change them dynamically or put them in a demon transformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T21:57:59-07:00","id":1457006,"title":"","content":"I suppose one of the relevant questions is whether he's a now-demonic spirit/consciousness that's still bound to a vampire body, or if he utterly transcended vampirism in the manner of certain antediluvians in that one Gehenna scenario. Are we dealing with Captain Howdy in Regan's body, or Pazuzu, king of the demons of wind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T03:02:42-07:00","id":1457013,"title":"","content":"Ravana struck down Dacian after becoming a Yama King, so there is precedent for such characters at least matching Antediluvians. I imagine them reaching Yama King levels, rather than becoming Fallen. Not all demons need to be the same power level though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T04:04:46-07:00","id":1457016,"title":"","content":"Depends on what sort of Demon, Mega wrym spirit seems more doable than Fallen. Although it's debatable if the curse of Caine can be circumvented and they're just cainites in denial by anyone Mi-kal-el was no angel afterall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T10:25:30-07:00","id":1457035,"title":"","content":"<i>House of Tremere</i> implied that Kupula and Saulot were operating on roughly the same playing field. Now whether Kupala itself is one of the Earthbound, a demon-god from the High Umbra, a powerful Wyrm spirit, or what have you is up to the individual Storyteller. I'd say that a vampire newly ascending to demonhood would probably be considerably less powerful than it is unless starting from antediluvian level, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T15:37:32-07:00","id":1462330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456910-azaneal-reaching-demonhood?p=1457035#post1457035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>House of Tremere</i> implied that Kupula and Saulot were operating on roughly the same playing field. Now whether Kupala itself is one of the Earthbound, a demon-god from the High Umbra, a powerful Wyrm spirit, or what have you is up to the individual Storyteller. I'd say that a vampire newly ascending to demonhood would probably be considerably less powerful than it is unless starting from antediluvian level, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> less powerful then it is? So you are saying its a downgrade? I cant imagine Azaneal agreeing to a deal that would make him weaker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T15:39:14-07:00","id":1462331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456910-azaneal-reaching-demonhood?p=1456914#post1456914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Azaneal and Mary the Black are both essentially &quot;here there be dragons&quot; characters, I think. Monsters like this are pretexts for never, ever commissioning writing on supplements that would take characters to certain locations until a novelist decides to send Beckett, Lucita, or Theo Bell there to save the day.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> nice Fargo reference <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T15:51:20-07:00","id":1462334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456910-azaneal-reaching-demonhood?p=1462330#post1462330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> less powerful then it is? So you are saying its a downgrade? I cant imagine Azaneal agreeing to a deal that would make him weaker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Less powerful than Kupula and similarly vast beings, not less powerful than he was before becoming a demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T16:12:44-07:00","id":1462343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456910-azaneal-reaching-demonhood?p=1462334#post1462334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Less powerful than Kupula and similarly vast beings, not less powerful than he was before becoming a demon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yeah definitely. didnt think he was on the same level as kupala but who is? You mentioned in another post that Saulot operated on the same level but i seriously doubt that. I got the impression that Kupala was wearing the pants in his relationship with the eldest. So i would consider him above ante level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T16:26:44-07:00","id":1462344,"title":"","content":"<i>Darkening Sky</i> implicitly puts Azaneal at fifth generation. He could also be sixth, if his childe is a diablerist. Or theoretically even higher, if she was a serial diablerist.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that becoming a demon frees Azaneal (or any such ascended Baali, like Mary the Black) from generational limits. The Curse of Caine isn't what they derive their power from anymore, so its limits no longer apply. They gain power however demons gain power.<br /> <br /> Power comes in lots of varieties, like being an incorporeal entity and no longer harmed by sunlight and fire, but in terms of &quot;innate&quot; supernatural power (that is, trait limits), Azaneal could have either gotten an instant boost to 8 or 9 (depending where his generation lay), or he could have just been happy to be a demon who no longer labored under a glass ceiling.<br /> <br /> By the Modern Nights, he's probably stronger than he was upon his ascension, but I don't see him as an equal to Saulot or Kupala. He's probably an 8 or 9 dot figure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T20:27:05-07:00","id":1462387,"title":"","content":"My own take would be that it is the Baali-equivalent for Golconda and that's it. Open path to higher level Disciplines and an easier time being yourself. Probably around the power level of a 4th gen Methuselah, maybe a little weaker than some. Daimonion 10 would by itself make an awesome difference without being enough to say for sure that he's more powerful than actual 4th gen Methuselahs.<br /> <br /> But yeah, it depends a lot. On what you think &quot;demon&quot; means in this context and what you think &quot;Methuselah Power&quot; is. Because if it is simply the natural progression of 4th gen in the table it is... kinda strong, I guess. And if 10th level Disciplines follow the trends of the lower levels, they're dangerous but not really THAT scary. And they may be even weaker than that.<br /> <br /> So what is this transcendence? Golconda? Yama-King? Incarna spirit? Angel/Fallen (weird, but who knows)? Each is a different host of consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T15:45:08-07:00","id":1462486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456910-azaneal-reaching-demonhood?p=1462344#post1462344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Darkening Sky</i> implicitly puts Azaneal at fifth generation. He could also be sixth, if his childe is a diablerist. Or theoretically even higher, if she was a serial diablerist.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that becoming a demon frees Azaneal (or any such ascended Baali, like Mary the Black) from generational limits. The Curse of Caine isn't what they derive their power from anymore, so its limits no longer apply. They gain power however demons gain power.<br /> <br /> Power comes in lots of varieties, like being an incorporeal entity and no longer harmed by sunlight and fire, but in terms of &quot;innate&quot; supernatural power (that is, trait limits), Azaneal could have either gotten an instant boost to 8 or 9 (depending where his generation lay), or he could have just been happy to be a demon who no longer labored under a glass ceiling.<br /> <br /> By the Modern Nights, he's probably stronger than he was upon his ascension, but I don't see him as an equal to Saulot or Kupala. He's probably an 8 or 9 dot figure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like your idea of what becoming a demon means. You will trancend the limits of caine's curse and the generational limits no longer apply! It makes sense if you didnt get an immediate boost of power but a higher potential. In theory azanael could, in a couple of centuries or milliennia, reach hights no vampire could, because vampires are hold back by the limits of their generation.<br /> <br /> But reading the comments it seems there is no definite answer to this in the lore and we can only speculate!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T15:45:08-07:00","id":1462487,"title":"","content":"Double post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T23:53:29-07:00","id":1464977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456910-azaneal-reaching-demonhood#post1456910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its mentioned in the wiki that he reached demonhood. Does anybody know how that happend?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is multiple ways. There was a daimonion power, depending on source 7 or 10 dots, that allows you to become a real actual demon with infernal ranking, there is also a dark thaumaturgy ritual for it.<br /> <br /> We do know that Nergal tried to achieve this, and apparently a few Baali have actually done it. Mary the black is an example of a demon becoming a Baali vampire, so the other way round.<br /> <br /> To what will that do - according to them rules you become a full fledged fallen with all that entails but was never fleshed out.<br /> <br /> My guess is, if you keep your vampiric body, and thus vitae, you keep your vampiric disciplines and powers and ADD the demon things, including your apocalyptic form and join the faction of demons that you dealt with most as Baali (Nergali - Ravener, Molochim - Faustian, order of inner light - Reconciler, Shaitiani - Luciferian....swarm and azaneali are a problem cause they arent dealing with demons much at all and are more abyss / wyrm oriented)<br /> <br /> The Daimonion 6 power already allows you to take on some forms of demonhood and demonic traits btw. And indeed many Baali try to achieve apotheosis and view becoming a Demon an indermediate step, as becoming a demon does make them truly immortal, though they will be thrown into the abyss if they are destroyed.<br /> <br /> A Baali become demon would be something like an abomination, just with a demon rather than a fera.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Darkening Sky</i> implicitly puts Azaneal at fifth generation.&quot; true that, and other sources claim Azaneal is 2nd generation, his personal history definitely makes him a pre flood vampire.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 10-23-2021, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T03:31:56-07:00","id":1464989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456910-azaneal-reaching-demonhood#post1456910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its mentioned in the wiki that he reached demonhood. Does anybody know how that happend?<br /> <br /> Also how powerful would he be once he became a demon? Are we talking ante level? Or possible even higher? Could he duke it out with Caine? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I never read up on demon lore so i am not sure how powerful demons are. I would presume as a newly made demon he wouldnt be high up the demon food chain. But still he transcended. That tells me his new form is far more powerful then he ever was as a vampire.<br /> <br /> There also seems to be a debate about his generation. Anything between second and fifth. Either way he was a powerful vampire. So is there any advantage if you reach demonhood, if you were a powerful vampire before? Would that put him higher in the new food chain?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is highly theoretical and there is no correct answer BUT: to be &quot;ante level&quot; a demon needs to be at least an Earthbound and even then just a few of those can match an antediluvian theoretical power (Kupala), the other &quot;ante level&quot; demons are the Archdukes, who might be even more powerful under the correct circumstances. Azaneal is not one of them.<br /> <br /> P.S.<br /> <br /> Azaneal is one of those characters invented without much thought about the overall lore of the WoD in a period when WW cared about consistency even less than it did afterwards...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T05:12:04-07:00","id":1465000,"title":"","content":"If we go for Fallen rules, power is relative. Outside some specific Earthbound rules there's no mechanical difference between them outside more points in the sheet. At the same time, since the character is already a vampire, its power as such pretty much counts.<br /> <br /> As a Fallen I think such vampires would become actually pretty low power demons, but they have their own Kindred powers added to compensate. This adds a nice twist that they're true immortals, but this current life is still insanely valuable.<br /> <br /> What could we make for them as rules? As a starting point I really think we have lower demonic power than a starting Fallen PC. Torment 1, Faith 1, no Lores. You still get the innate abilities of the Fallen, that add a huge amount of options to a character already powerful, and your Apocalyptic Form that is just a big bonus with no drawbacks. The ability of making your current followers into Thralls is also pretty powerful.<br /> <br /> From this I think since it is an apotheosis, a few bonuses could be added. Title is just a social background for demons, but still a pretty useful one. A thrall that becomes a full fledged demon and gets some Title right out of the bat is a very clear recognition of its power and service. Remembrance for this character wouldn't be memories of the War, but would fit nicely as a reward in the form of ancient knowledge.<br /> <br /> That aside, I think the knowledge of Disciplines should carry on in a special way. If this character is ever sent to Hell they're pretty weakened, but they have more to offer to Kindred than any other Demon, as they can teach Disciplines. One idea I have is that they could have exclusive access to a Lore of Caine, with effects like Imbuing Disciplines on Thralls, being able to possess vampires upon returning and recover their own Disciplines, producing Vitae and other thematic effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}